00:09:03.826 --> 00:09:07.363
CITY'S MOST ICONIC PROJECTS. FROM THE REVITALIZATION OF PIER

00:09:07.363 --> 00:09:11.567
ONE TO THE CREATION OF CRANE COVE PARK AND THE INNOVATION AT

00:09:11.567 --> 00:09:15.772
MISSION ROCK AND PIER 70. >> BUT BYRON WAS MORE THAN A

00:09:15.772 --> 00:09:19.242
LEADER. HE WAS A MENTOR, AN ADVOCATE

00:09:19.242 --> 00:09:23.312
AND A BUILDER OF COMMUNITY. HE BELIEVED DEEPLY IN EQUITY,

00:09:23.312 --> 00:09:26.912
PARTICULARLY IN UPLIFTING THE BAY VIEW.

00:09:27.183 --> 00:09:30.853
AND HE LED WITH MORE THAN MOST INTEGRITY AND HEART.

00:09:30.853 --> 00:09:34.457
HIS WORK LIVES ON NOT ONLY IN THE PLACES HE HELPED CREATE

00:09:34.457 --> 00:09:38.861
BUT IN THE VALUES AND SPIRIT HE INSTILLED IN THOSE AROUND HIM.

00:09:38.861 --> 00:09:42.398
SAN FRANCISCO IS BETTER BECAUSE OF BYRON.

00:09:42.398 --> 00:09:45.934
I AM GRATEFUL FOR HIS LIFELONG COMMITMENT TO OUR CITY AND I

00:09:45.934 --> 00:09:49.605
EXTEND MY DEEPEST CONDOLENCES TO HIS WIFE ANDREA AND THEIR

00:09:49.605 --> 00:09:55.500
SONS JUSTIN AND ZANE. MAY HIS MEMORY CONTINUE TO

00:09:56.145 --> 00:10:00.149
GUIDE US AS WE BUILD A MORE INCLUSIVE AND CONNECTED SAN

00:10:00.149 --> 00:10:01.150
FRANCISCO. >> THE REST I SUBMIT.

